 min-w-0"><div class="stack max-w-conversation mx-auto flex min-w-0 flex-col items-center overflow-visible"><div class="min-w-0 w-full"><div><div class="prose prose-trimmed ur-markdown citation-aware"><div class="ur-sm mb-4 flex flex-col gap-6" style="--ur-sm-fade-duration: 150ms;"><p dir="auto">What I changed:</p><ul dir="ltr" class="list-inside whitespace-normal [li_&amp;]:ps-6 list-disc"><li class="py-1 [&amp;&gt;p]:inline"><strong>Certificate degree:</strong> “Computer Science, Electronics and Physics” → <strong>“Computer Science, Mathematics”</strong>, to match your title page and roll code 26CSMM19. If Mathematics is actually the wrong one, tell me and I’ll flip it to Electronics and Physics instead.</li><li class="py-1 [&amp;&gt;p]:inline"><strong>Typo:</strong> deleted the stray <code>nesd</code> in the 4.4.2 CSS (<code>margin-bottom: 15px;nesd</code>).</li><li class="py-1 [&amp;&gt;p]:inline"><strong>TOC:</strong> now starts on its own fresh page. I re-checked pagination after the fix — the TOC page numbers are <strong>still correct</strong> (1.0 on printed p. 1, 8.0 References on printed p. 83, 90 PDF pages total).</li><li class="py-1 [&amp;&gt;p]:inline"><strong>Missing 4.2.1 HTML:</strong> added the full <code>events.html</code> code under 4.2.1, matching the version used in 4.3.1.</li><li class="py-1 [&amp;&gt;p]:inline"><strong>Screenshot placeholders:</strong> replaced all “Insert screenshots of / from <span class="ur-sm-atom"><span data-state="closed" data-slot="hover-card-trigger"><span role="button" tabindex="0" data-testid="user-pill" class="font-semibold mx-0.5 cursor-pointer align-baseline transition-colors no-underline"><span class="decoration-text-secondary underline decoration-dotted decoration-1 underline-offset-[18.5%] [text-decoration-skip-ink:none] [text-underline-position:from-font]">MongoDB</span></span></span></span> / showing…” instructions in 4.3.5, 4.4.5, 5.2 and 6.3 with a clean <strong>“Screenshot to be added.”</strong> line, and 