e_this_to_a_long_random_value_2026</span></code></pre></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="min-w-0"><div class="markdown-content min-w-0"><div class="stack max-w-conversation mx-auto flex min-w-0 flex-col items-center overflow-visible"><div class="min-w-0 w-full"><div><div class="prose prose-trimmed ur-markdown citation-aware"><div class="ur-sm mb-4 flex flex-col gap-6" style="--ur-sm-fade-duration: 150ms;"><p dir="auto">With a note explaining what each line does.</p><ol dir="ltr" class="list-inside whitespace-normal [li_&amp;]:ps-6 list-decimal" start="2"><li class="py-1 [&amp;&gt;p]:inline"><strong>Section 5.0 Database → printed p. 87</strong> — new block <strong>“DATABASE CONNECTION — .env FILE”</strong>, right before 5.2, because that's where <code>MONGODB_URI</code> is used to connect to <code>collegeEventDB</code>. It points back to the same file in 4.1.4, so the values aren't shown as two different files.</li></ol><p dir="auto"><strong>Also fixed:</strong> adding those blocks shifted everything after p. 20 by 1–2 pages, so I re-measured and updated the TOC (e.g. 4.1.5: 20 → 21, 4.4.5: 84 → 85, References: 90 → 92). TOC numbers are still in the right-aligned column — verified, all ending at the same 540.2 pt.</p><p dir="auto">⚠️ One caution: this file now contains your real <code>JWT_SECRET</code>. Don't share the report publicly / upload it anywhere online — change that secret value in your real <code>.env</code> before deployment, since anyone with it can forge login tokens.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-conversation"></div><div class="group/assistant-message-actions max-w-conversation mx-auto flex min-h-11 flex-wrap items-center select-none"><div data-slot="flexbox" class="min-h-0 min-w-0 flex items-center gap-x-1 gap-y-1 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:-ms-1"><div class="flex items-center gap-1 ecto-message-action-cascade"><div class="contents"><button aria-label="Like 